    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0238" n="150" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg150"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Peking,
                                China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-03-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 22, 1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1544.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose translation of
                    a set of mining regulations issued for the province of Hu-nan, and which have
                    received Imperial approval.</p>
                <p>These appear to me so flagrant a violation of the provisions of our treaty that I
                    have filed with the foreign office a formal protest against them, copy of which
                    I also inclose. The English and German ministers here inform me that they have
                    taken like action.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>



